// Chief Marlow — the "Clear the Deck" bounty (quest 2): put Vex down, report
// back, get paid a Maintenance Keycard (item 5). The offer and turn-in both
// check npc_defeated, so beating Vex before taking the bounty still pays out.

title: entry
---
<<if quest_state(2, "Success")>>
    <<jump already_done>>
<<elseif quest_state(2, "InProgress")>>
    <<jump inprogress>>
<<else>>
    <<jump offer>>
<<endif>>
===

title: inprogress
---
<<if npc_defeated("intro.vex")>>
    <<jump turnin>>
<<else>>
    <<jump inprogress_waiting>>
<<endif>>
===

title: offer
---
<<if npc_defeated("intro.vex")>>
    <<jump offer_downed>>
<<else>>
    <<jump offer_pending>>
<<endif>>
===

title: already_done
---
$npc: Deck's been quiet since you put Vex on the plates. Keep that keycard handy — it opens more doors than you'd think.
===

title: inprogress_waiting
---
$npc: Vex is still strutting around the plaza like he owns it. The keycard's yours the moment that changes.
===

title: offer_pending
---
$npc: See that red-suited thug by the plaza? Vex. He's been shaking down every courier on this deck and my hands are tied. Put him down a peg and there's a maintenance keycard in it for you.
-> I'll handle Vex
    <<set_quest 2 InProgress>>
    $npc: Watch yourself — he doesn't fight fair, and he keeps a drone at his back. Come see me when it's done.
-> Not my problem
    <<jump declined>>
===

title: offer_downed
---
$npc: Word is somebody already put Vex on the deck plates. That was you, wasn't it? I was about to post a bounty on him — say the word and it's yours.
-> That was me
    <<set_quest 2 InProgress>>
    <<jump turnin>>
-> Not my problem
    <<jump declined>>
===

title: declined
---
$npc: Then keep your credits out of his reach, and don't say I didn't warn you.
===

title: turnin
---
<<give_item 5>>
<<set_quest 2 Success>>
$npc: So the deck finally goes quiet. A deal's a deal — here's the maintenance keycard. It'll open doors most people never get to see.
===
